 East, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Soul City Social Club (Toronto, Canada)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/soulcity/"},"performer":"Soul City Social Club (Toronto, Canada)"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Dinner with Friends Gratitude Party! (Cocktails and Conversations) (Oct. 18th) ","url":"https://www.meetup.com/soulcity/events/316611307/","description":"Hello everyone,\n\nI'd like to invite you out to our **Dinner with Friends Gratitude Party!**\n\n-Reserved seating, friendly people, good conversation and great food awaits!\n\nSo please plan to join us if you can :)\n\n\\*Joined by my other groups too; so we can anticipate a fantastic evening\n\n**Time: 6:30 p.m. -9:30 p.m.**\n**Location:** La Carnita - Good Fortune Bar (Main Floor)\n**Address:** 130 Eglinton Ave. Toronto, ON M4P 2X9\n\nEvent Details Bellow:\n\nSincerely,\n\nSteve Flemming\n(Organizer/Host)\n\nEvent Details:\n**Dinner with Friends Gratitude Party! (Dinner, Cocktails and Conversations) (October 18th)**\n-The great thing about this dinner party is you're free to move around to different tables and meet the other members too throughout the evening\n\n**Dinner Party Topics** may include but not limited too: Travel, Culture, Spirituality, Relationships, Modern Dating, Work/Life balance, Life after Marriage, Dating Apps, Comedy, History, Art, Technology, Future of A.I., Economy, Music, Movies, Sports, Fashion, Hobbies, Books, Psychology, Philosophy, History, Pop Culture, Theatre, etc.)\n\n**Arrival Time:**\n\\*Join us any time between 6:30 pm and 7:15 pm (if you can) for a fun and highly interactive evening as we get to know the members over dinner and great conversations (of your choice)\nEvent goes until roughly 9:30 pm\n\n**Event Fee:**\n5 dollars (cash only please) (HST included)\nor in advance by e transfer to **[steveflemming11@gmail.com](http://steveflemming11@gmail.com/)**\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\n**Friendly Reminder:**\n\\*One beverage or appetizer minimum to support the venue- this is greatly appreciated :)\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\n**Parking Available:**\n\\*Plenty of free street parking on Eglinton and (Residential area south/east of venue for free)\n**Close to Subway Station:**\n\\*Also right beside the Yonge/Eglinton subway station :)\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-","startDate":"2026-10-18T22:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"La Carnita","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"130 Eglinton Ave.  East, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Soul City Social Club (Toronto, Canada)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/soulcity/"},"performer":"Soul City Social Club (Toronto, Canada)"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Brunch/Lunch at Old Mill - 12 spots","url":"https://www.meetup.com/north-york-55-womens-group/events/313929547/","description":"Ladies, join us for a beautiful autumn brunch at the historic Old Mill on Sunday, October 18th.\n\nWe’ll enjoy their all-you-can-eat brunch, surrounded by the gorgeous fall colours along the Humber River. After brunch, anyone who’s up for it can take a little stroll along the river trails.\n\nI’m looking forward to great food, great conversation, and lots of laughter with wonderful women.\n\nPrice (tax & 18% gratuity included) -$95.00\n\nPLEASE READ:\nSIGN-UP PROCESS\nSTEPS:\nHow Our New Process Works:\n\nRSVP to Join Waitlist\n\n* When you RSVP, you'll be added to our waitlist, which is your way of expressing interest in joining us.\nSecure Your Spot\n\n* E-transfer $95.00 to: fabulousover50@hotmail.com. Include the event name in your message. If your email name differs from your Meetup profile, please let me know. Please note, $95.00 is non refundable or non transferable\n\nConfirmation\n\n* Once payment is received, I'll move you from the waitlist to \"going\" - spots are secured in order of payment received.\n\nEvent Capacity\n\n* When maximum capacity is reached, RSVPs will close. Please stay on the waitlist as spots may open due to cancellations.\n\nManage Your RSVP\n\n* If plans change, please remove yourself from the waitlist to allow others the opportunity to join.\n\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nPOSITIVE GROUP POLICIES\n\nMeet Someone New:\n\nEvery meetup is a chance to make a new friend! We encourage everyone to sit with someone different each time.\n\nOpen Seating\n* Seats are first come, first serve - no saving seats. This helps everyone feel welcome and included.\nWarm Welcome\n* If you see someone new or alone, invite them to join your table or conversation.\nPositive Vibes Only\n* We celebrate kindness, encouragement, and support in all our interactions.\nRespectful Listening\n* Everyone's voice matters. Listen with respect & curiosity.\n\nLet's make every meetup a chance to expand our circle of friends.\n\nA smile and a hello can make someone's day - let's be that person for each other.\n\nTrying something new can be scary - thank-you for being brave and open to meeting new people! We are all here to connect, so let's make sure no one feels left out!\n\nWarmest Regards\nMirella","startDate":"2026-10-18T17:15:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-5-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Old Mill","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"21 Old Mill Rd, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Fabulous Women Over 50 Club","url":"https://www.meetup.com/north-york-55-womens-group/"},"performer":"Fabulous Women Over 50 Club"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":" 🌿 FALL WALK -  Walk: Tommy Thompson Park (Come See The Skyline) 🐦 - 12KM","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-movies-and-social-group/events/316183191/","description":"# 🍂🐦 Fall Walk: Tommy Thompson Park 🌊\n\n### Wildlife, Lake Views & One of Toronto's Best Fall Walks\n\nLooking for a walk that feels like you've left the city without actually leaving Toronto?\n\nJoin us for a fall walk through **Tommy Thompson Park**, one of Toronto's most unique outdoor spaces.\nThe park is famous for its wildlife and birding, with **more than 300 species recorded**, as well as its beautiful views across Lake Ontario and back toward the Toronto skyline.\nIn the fall, the cooler air and quieter trails make this a particularly nice time to explore the park. We'll follow the trails toward the **lighthouse**, take a break along the way, and then make our way back.\n\nIt's a **long walk**, but the terrain is generally easy. The goal is to enjoy the scenery, get some fresh air, and spend a few hours walking and talking with other people.\n\n📱 Don't forget to join our **WhatsApp Group – [CLICK HERE](https://chat.whatsapp.com/H59mSCbsAi018gYANrKAnc)**\n\n***\n\n## 🚶‍♂️ What We'll Do\n\nWe'll meet near the pavilion and begin our walk through Tommy Thompson Park.\n\nAlong the way we'll:\n\n* Explore the park's trails 🌿\n* Look for birds and other wildlife 🐦\n* Enjoy views of Lake Ontario 🌊\n* Take in the Toronto skyline 🌆\n* Make our way toward the lighthouse\n* Stop for a break and some photos 📸\n* Loop back to the pavilion\n\nThe walk will take approximately **3 hours, including a break**.\nThis is a longer walk, so you should be comfortable walking at a steady pace for several hours.\n**No dogs are permitted in the park.**\n\n***\n\n## 🍁 Fall Weather & Expectations\n\nThis is an outdoor walk, and Tommy Thompson can be exposed to the wind coming off Lake Ontario.\nPlease dress appropriately for the weather and bring comfortable walking shoes.\n\nThe trail isn't particularly difficult, but **the distance is the challenge**. If you're not comfortable being on your feet and walking steadily for around three hours, this may not be the right walk for you.\n\n***\n\n## 🧢 Meetup Details\n\n📍 **Meetup Location:** Near the pavilion and bathrooms\n🫎 **Look for me in my Moose Hat!**\n⏰ **Meetup Time: 11:00 AM sharp**\nI will only wait **5 minutes.**\n**Early is on time. On time is late.**\n🏁 **End Point:** Tommy Thompson Park Pavilion\n\n***\n\n## 🎟️ Meetup Fee\n\n**$5 cash in person or e-transfer**\n📧 **mathewmaclean@hotmail.com**\nThis fee helps support the group and allows us to continue organizing events throughout Toronto.\n\n***\n\n## 🍔 After the Walk\n\nOnce we've finished, you're welcome to join us for lunch at **Wendy's or Tim Hortons** nearby.\nIt's completely optional, but it's a great chance to sit down, refuel, and continue the conversation after the walk.\n\n***\n\n## 🎒 What to Bring\n\n💧 Water\n👟 Comfortable walking shoes\n🥪 A snack\n🧥 A fall jacket or sweater\n📸 Camera or phone for photos\n\n***\n\n## 🌈 Who Is This For?\n\nThis walk is great for:\n\n* People who enjoy nature and wildlife 🐦\n* Anyone interested in birdwatching\n* People who love waterfront walks\n* Anyone looking for a longer social walk\n* People who want to explore somewhere different in Toronto\n* Anyone who enjoys getting outside and meeting new people\n\nThe activity is the container. **The people you meet along the way are the real experience.**\n\nYou're welcome to RSVP ahead of time or just show up on the day if you're unsure about your schedule.\nSometimes things happen and events may need to be cancelled or changed, so please keep an eye on the event page for updates.\n\n👤 **Organizer: Mathew**\n\nQuestions? Post on the event wall or email **torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com**\n\n**Come for the wildlife.** 🐦\n**Stay for the conversation.**\n**Leave with a new connection — and maybe a new friend.** 🍂💛","startDate":"2026-10-18T15:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Tommy Thompson Park Pavilion -TTC","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"9 Leslie Lookout Park, Toronto, ON M4M 3H7, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-movies-and-social-group/"},"performer":"Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"🔥Toronto Founder Walk | Marketers, Entrepreneurs & Business Owners","url":"https://www.meetup.com/internet-marketing-strategy-group/events/316756568/","description":"A lot of people in this group work with entrepreneurs every day — or are entrepreneurs themselves.\nAgency owners, marketers, consultants, freelancers, creators, startup founders and business owners often end up at the same conferences and seminars...\n…but don't necessarily get much time to actually know one another.\nSo instead of another marketing presentation, we're trying something simpler:\n\\# 🚶 Toronto Founder Walk\nA casual Sunday walk along Toronto's Harbourfront where entrepreneurs, marketers and business owners can meet through natural conversation.\nNo slides.\nNo speakers.\nNo sales presentation.\nNo forced networking exercises.\nJust:\n**Walk. Talk. Meet someone interesting.**\n\\#\\#\\# The idea\nI've been involved with entrepreneur and community events in Toronto since 2016, and this new series grew out of the **18,000-member Toronto Entrepreneurs & Start-ups Facebook community**.\nOne thing I've noticed over the years is that the best connections rarely come from exchanging as many business cards as possible.\nThey usually happen when you spend enough time talking to someone to discover:\n\\> “Oh\\, this person actually thinks about things in an interesting way\\.”\nThat's what we're trying to create.\n\n**🚩Important: Meetup RSVP ≠ confirmed spot**\n**Keep your Meetup RSVP as Going so the event stays visible here. You will get link to a short application after you RSVP.**\n\n📍Meetup Location: Simcoe Wavedeck sign\n**📅Sunday schedule**\n**🕛4:45 PM — Arrive / check in**\n**🕛5:00 PM — Introductions**\nTell us who you are, what you're working on and one interesting way you're using—or want to use—AI.\n**🕛5:15 PM — Walk begins**\nWe'll rotate conversations and introduce a few AI discussion prompts along the route.\n**🕛Around 6:15 PM — Official finish**\nMany stay afterwards to network. Some people may grab food or a drink afterward.\n\n**🏃Running late?**\nDon't give up on coming.\nApproved guests can join our Sunday Walk WhatsApp group. Once we're moving, we'll share our live location so late arrivals can catch up.\n\nWe'll help make introductions at the start, but this is intentionally informal.\nPossible conversations might include:\n\n* What's actually working in marketing right now?\n* Growing an agency or service business\n* AI and automation\n* Customer acquisition\n* Entrepreneurship\n* Building a personal brand\n* Sales\n* Hiring\n* What you're currently working on\n* Or something completely unrelated to work\n\nYou don't have to talk marketing for 75 minutes.\nThe activity is simply there to make meeting people easier.\n\\#\\#\\# Who this is for\nEspecially relevant for:\n\n* Entrepreneurs\n* Agency owners\n* Digital marketers\n* Consultants\n* Freelancers\n* Creators\n* Startup founders\n* Business owners\n* Growth and marketing professionals\n\nYou don't need to sell marketing services.\nYou just need to be genuinely interested in meeting other people who build, market or operate businesses.\n\\#\\#\\# What this is NOT\nThis is not:\n\n* A lead-generation mixer\n* A seminar\n* A pitching session\n* A place to aggressively collect prospects\n\nIf your main objective is to distribute business cards to everyone, this probably isn't the right event.\nIf you'd enjoy meeting a few thoughtful people and seeing where the conversation goes, it probably is.\n\\#\\#\\# ☕ Optional afterward\nWe'll finish the formal walk around 6:15 PM.\nAnyone who wants can continue for coffee, food or a drink nearby.\n\\#\\#\\# 🎟 How to reserve your spot\n**Meetup RSVP does not confirm attendance.**\nPlease register through Luma:\n👉 [https://superr.ca/mmevents](https://superr.ca/mmevents)\nWe keep the walks relatively small, so please release your spot if your plans change.\n\\#\\#\\# 📱 Future events\nFor first notice of upcoming casual entrepreneur events, join **TES Social on WhatsApp**:\n👉 **[https://biz1.ca/wa](https://biz1.ca/wa)**\nUpcoming formats may include:\n\n* Founder walks\n* Small dinners\n* Breakfasts\n* Marketing/AI discussions\n* Sports\n* Wellness\n* Social activities\n\n\\#\\#\\# 🙌 Want to host or contribute?\nWe're looking for people interested in:\n\n* Hosting\n* Co-hosting\n* Photography\n* Video\n* Reels\n* Venue partnerships\n* Activities\n* Event support\n\n👉 **[https://superr.ca/host](https://biz1.ca/host)**\nCome curious.\nLeave the pitch at home.\nHopefully meet someone worth seeing again.\n#DigitalMarketingToronto #TorontoEntrepreneurs #FounderWalk #MarketingCommunity #TESSocial\n\n***📸Photo, Video & Audio Notice:*** *By registering for or attending this event, you acknowledge that photos, video and audio recordings may be captured during the event. You consent to Superr / TES Social using your image, likeness, voice and comments in event recaps, social media, promotional materials and other community content. If you prefer not to be photographed, filmed or recorded, please let the host know before the event and we’ll do our best to accommodate you.*","startDate":"2026-10-18T20:59:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-3-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Simcoe WaveDeck","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"243 X Queens Quay W, Toronto, ON M5J 2G8, Canada, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"🦄Digital Marketing Toronto","url":"https://www.meetup.com/internet-marketing-strategy-group/"},"performer":"🦄Digital Marketing Toronto"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Toronto East Weekend Gaming @ Face-to-Face Games","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-heavy-boardgamers/events/316231807/","description":"Welcome to the Sunday meetup for Toronto Heavy Boardgamers @ Face-to-Face Games!\n\nThe purpose of this event is to meet up to play heavier / longer board games, and have fun while doing it! We will start off small and if there is sufficient interest we will add capacity for future events.\n\n**Scheduling details:**\n\n\\- If you have a specific game that you would like to post for\\, feel free to do so in comments\\. In your post\\, include the name of the game\\, number of players needed for the game\\, whether you are offering a teach or not\\, and the start time \\(please try to start before noon if possible\\)\\.\n\n\\- If you would like to join a specific game that has already been posted\\, feel free to comment on it confirming your participation\\. Make sure you have noted the details posted by the host\\.\n\n\\- You are of course also welcome to organize / join games onsite on the day itself\\, assuming sufficient players / tables are available\n\n**Rules around COVID:**\n\n\\- Given this is a public event\\, we respectfully ask that only i\\) fully vaccinated individuals\\, and ii\\) those not exhibiting any COVID symptoms\\, participate\\. This requirement may change in the future based on provincial guidelines and group requirements\n\n**Admission Fee:**\n\n\\- There are no table fees for this event","startDate":"2026-10-18T15:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Face to Face Games","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"1398 Danforth Ave, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Heavy Boardgamers","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-heavy-boardgamers/"},"performer":"Toronto Heavy Boardgamers"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Tantric Family Constellation: Temple of Love & Money","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-tantra-circle/events/316757999/","description":"**TANTRIC FAMILY CONSTELLATIONS**\n**Tantric Temple Mysteries**\n\n**This is the project overview only.**\n**Themes and dates may change.**\n\n**To find the exact topic, date and register, please join:**\n\n**t.me/TorontoTantra**\n**t.me/AndyTherapist**\n\n**⸻**\n\n**About this event**\n\n**Tantric Family Constellations is a group practice combining Archetypal / Family Constellations with a living tantric Temple space.**\n\n**Each meeting has its own theme.**\n\n**For example:**\n\n**Love & Money • Ancient Languages of Love • Love & Loneliness • Masculine & Feminine • Desire & Freedom • Relationship Patterns**\n\n**The theme gives us a field to explore — but every participant discovers their own personal story inside it.**\n\n**⸻**\n\n**Part 1 — Discover your pattern**\n\n**We begin by exploring different dimensions of the evening’s theme together.**\n\n**Then each participant goes through a mini-constellation to see their own pattern, model or hidden dynamic.**\n\n**Instead of only thinking about the question, you can see how its different forces are arranged for you:**\n\n**What attracts you?**\n**What do you avoid?**\n**Where does your energy stop?**\n**What are you moving toward?**\n\n**This creates a personal map for the second part of the evening.**\n\n**⸻**\n\n**Part 2 — Enter the Temple**\n\n**Then we open the Tantric Temple.**\n\n**The constellation points become living centers in the space.**\n\n**Participants are free to move between them, following their own inner process.**\n\n**You may stay with one energy, move toward another, step away, return, observe what happens in your body, or allow yourself to gradually absorb a quality that previously felt distant.**\n\n**At the same time, you encounter other participants moving through their own paths.**\n\n**Through presence, movement and consensual interaction, the personal constellation becomes a living group field.**\n\n**There is no fixed choreography and no need to perform.**\n\n**You follow your own rhythm.**\n\n**The practice is about allowing yourself to experience, embody and integrate the different energies of the constellation rather than only understand them intellectually.**\n\n**⸻**\n\n**Why “Temple”?**\n\n**The Temple is a temporary tantric space where symbolic and archetypal energies can be experienced through the body, movement and connection with others.**\n\n**The journey is individual, but it happens inside a shared field.**\n\n**You may discover that a quality which looked abstract during the constellation becomes much more understandable once you can actually move toward it, stay with it and experience it in contact with others.**\n\n**⸻**\n\n**No previous constellation or tantra experience is required.**\n\n**Participation is voluntary, and you can always choose your own level of involvement and contact.**\n\n**The space is based on:**\n\n**consent • respect • confidentiality • personal boundaries • freedom of movement**\n\n**This is a transpersonal personal-growth practice.**\n\n**Details, themes, dates and registration:**\n**t.me/TorontoTantra**\n\n**TICKETS**\n\n1. **Regular Ticket — $100 CAD**\n1. **Early Bird Ticket — $65 CAD**\n**If you register and pay before August 31.**\n**3. Supportive Ticket — $55 CAD**\n**For people with limited financial resources.**\n**4. Bring a Friend — $150 CAD for 2 people**\n\n**If the price is too much for you, send a personal message on Telegram: t.me/AndyTherapist to ask about volunteer options.**\n\n**HOW TO PAY**\n\n**Send an Interac e-Transfer to:**\n**andy.litvinov@gmail.com**\n**After payment, send a screenshot of the confirmation to: t.me/AndyTherapist**\n**Please mention which event you are registering for.**\n\n**After registration, you will be added to the participants’ group.**\n\n**If you have any questions, feel free to message:**\n**t.me/AndyTherapist**\n**Toronto Tantra community:**\n**t.me/TorontoTantra**","startDate":"2026-10-18T23:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"","addressRegion":"","addressCountry":""}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"T.me/TorontoTantra Circle","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-tantra-circle/"},"performer":"T.me/TorontoTantra Circle"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Tantra Toronto","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-tantra-circle/events/316758113/","description":"**To register and get details please send a message beforehand to the group: t.me/TorontoTantra, t.me/AndyTherapist.**\n**Registration a few days before the event is required.**\n\n**Sunday Aug 16th 7-10pm**\n\n**Doors at 6:50**\n**Doors close at 7:10.**\n\n**WHAT TO EXPECT**\n\n**6:50 doors open**\n**7:10 pm doors close**\n**7:20- 9:40pm 8 we drop in, share, make requests on what we'd like to learn + experience & get to practice!**\n**10pm event closes**\n\n**ABOUT THE EVENT**\n**Come get the education in sxuality you never got, but wish you had 💥**\n\n**The education we get in sxuality from school is so limited. We grow up seeking information often in all the wrong places.**\n\n**What if the conversation around sexuality was brought out in the open? What if it wasn't fraught with shame, with dogma?**\n\n**What if we learnt to identify our desires, our boundaries, how to have safe conversations around intimacy and this was common place?**\n\n**Tantric Drop ins is a community oriented workshop where you can come in as you are, drop in with community, rest, relax & play all the while learning these super important skills as well as some beginner friendly tantric practices.**\n**EXCHANGE: 55cad.**","startDate":"2026-10-18T23:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"","addressRegion":"","addressCountry":""}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"T.me/TorontoTantra Circle","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-tantra-circle/"},"performer":"T.me/TorontoTantra Circle"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"⭐Toronto AI Social Walk | Founders Builders & Business Owners","url":"https://www.meetup.com/greater-toronto-travel-and-social-club/events/316755853/","description":"**🔥Everyone is talking about AI. Let's talk about what we're actually doing with it.**\nAt our last Founder Walk, something unexpected happened.\nThe conversation kept coming back to AI.\nOne person was exploring AI agents for businesses.\nSomeone else was thinking about automating workflows for small and medium-sized companies.\nWe talked about using AI to evaluate employee onboarding, browser agents that can operate websites for you, AI-generated music, investing, software development and where actual business opportunities might be emerging.\nNobody planned an AI discussion.\nIt just happened.\n\n**🚩Important: Meetup RSVP ≠ confirmed spot**\n**Keep your Meetup RSVP as Going so the event stays visible here. You will get link to a short application after you RSVP.**\n\nSo this Sunday we're leaning into it.\n**⭐Toronto AI Walk⭐**\nA small group of founders, builders, professionals and curious people walking Toronto's waterfront and talking about:\n**What are you actually using AI for?**\n**What have you built?**\n**Which tools are genuinely useful?**\n**Where is AI still overhyped?**\n**What business opportunities are appearing?**\n**What workflows should already be automated?**\n**What will become possible if today's AI gets 10× better?**\n\nThis is **not a presentation or AI conference.**\nThere are no speakers.\nNo panels.\nNo sitting through someone's 45-minute pitch.\nAnd you don't have to be an AI expert.\nWe're deliberately keeping the group small enough that everyone can participate.\n\n**Some of the conversations from our last walk**\n\n1. One attendee was exploring creating custom AI workflow systems for small businesses.\n2. Another wanted to better understand how AI could solve problems outside the traditional technology industry.\n\nWe discussed using AI to evaluate sales training and employee onboarding, AI browser agents, automation, music, investing and entirely new businesses.\nThis week we'll use a few prompts to take those conversations further.\n\n📍Meetup Location: Simcoe Wavedeck sign\n**📅Sunday schedule**\n**🕛4:45 PM — Arrive / check in**\n**🕛5:00 PM — Introductions**\nTell us who you are, what you're working on and one interesting way you're using—or want to use—AI.\n**🕛5:15 PM — Walk begins**\nWe'll rotate conversations and introduce a few AI discussion prompts along the route.\n**🕛Around 6:15 PM — Official finish**\nMany stay afterwards to network. Some people may grab food or a drink afterward.\n\n**🏃Running late?**\nDon't give up on coming.\nApproved guests can join our Sunday Walk WhatsApp group. Once we're moving, we'll share our live location so late arrivals can catch up.\n\n**❓Who should come?**\nYou might be:\n\n* building with AI;\n* using AI inside an existing business;\n* working in technology;\n* exploring an AI startup;\n* trying to automate your work;\n* curious about where the opportunities are;\n* simply interested in learning from people experimenting with it.\n\nYou do **not** need to be an AI expert.\nCome curious.\nBring one thing you've learned and one thing you're trying to figure out.\n**No hard selling.**\n**💌RSVP: [https://superr.ca/msevent](https://superr.ca/msevent)**\n\nWe're also using the Superr Social WhatsApp Community to announce upcoming walks, dinners, sports, activities and other casual gatherings first:\n👉[https://superr.ca/mwa](https://superr.ca/mwa)\n\n#TorontoEntrepreneurs #TorontoFounders #FounderWalk #EntrepreneurCommunity #TESSocial\n\n***📸Photo, Video & Audio Notice:*** *By registering for or attending this event, you acknowledge that photos, video and audio recordings may be captured during the event. You consent to Superr / TES Social using your image, likeness, voice and comments in event recaps, social media, promotional materials and other community content. If you prefer not to be photographed, filmed or recorded, please let the host know before the event and we’ll do our best to accommodate you.*","startDate":"2026-10-18T20:45:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Queens Quay","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"CA","streetAddress":"88 queens quay west ,, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer