nday we're leaning into it.\n**⭐Toronto AI Walk⭐**\nA small group of founders, builders, professionals and curious people walking Toronto's waterfront and talking about:\n**What are you actually using AI for?**\n**What have you built?**\n**Which tools are genuinely useful?**\n**Where is AI still overhyped?**\n**What business opportunities are appearing?**\n**What workflows should already be automated?**\n**What will become possible if today's AI gets 10× better?**\n\nThis is **not a presentation or AI conference.**\nThere are no speakers.\nNo panels.\nNo sitting through someone's 45-minute pitch.\nAnd you don't have to be an AI expert.\nWe're deliberately keeping the group small enough that everyone can participate.\n\n**Some of the conversations from our last walk**\n\n1. One attendee was exploring creating custom AI workflow systems for small businesses.\n2. Another wanted to better understand how AI could solve problems outside the traditional technology industry.\n\nWe discussed using AI to evaluate sales training and employee onboarding, AI browser agents, automation, music, investing and entirely new businesses.\nThis week we'll use a few prompts to take those conversations further.\n\n📍Meetup Location: Simcoe Wavedeck sign\n**📅Sunday schedule**\n**🕛4:45 PM — Arrive / check in**\n**🕛5:00 PM — Introductions**\nTell us who you are, what you're working on and one interesting way you're using—or want to use—AI.\n**🕛5:15 PM — Walk begins**\nWe'll rotate conversations and introduce a few AI discussion prompts along the route.\n**🕛Around 6:15 PM — Official finish**\nMany stay afterwards to network. Some people may grab food or a drink afterward.\n\n**🏃Running late?**\nDon't give up on coming.\nApproved guests can join our Sunday Walk WhatsApp group. Once we're moving, we'll share our live location so late arrivals can catch up.\n\n**❓Who should come?**\nYou might be:\n\n* building with AI;\n* using AI inside an existing business;\n* working in technology;\n* exploring an AI startup;\n* trying to automate your work;\n* curious about where the opportunities are;\n* simply interested in learning from people experimenting with it.\n\nYou do **not** need to be an AI expert.\nCome curious.\nBring one thing you've learned and one thing you're trying to figure out.\n**No hard selling.**\n**💌RSVP: [https://superr.ca/msevent](https://superr.ca/msevent)**\n\nWe're also using the Superr Social WhatsApp Community to announce upcoming walks, dinners, sports, activities and other casual gatherings first:\n👉[https://superr.ca/mwa](https://superr.ca/mwa)\n\n#TorontoEntrepreneurs #TorontoFounders #FounderWalk #EntrepreneurCommunity #TESSocial\n\n***📸Photo, Video \u0026 Audio Notice:*** *By registering for or attending this event, you acknowledge that photos, video and audio recordings may be captured during the event. You consent to Superr / TES Social using your image, likeness, voice and comments in event recaps, social media, promotional materials and other community content. If you prefer not to be photographed, filmed or recorded, please let the host know before the event and we’ll do our best to accommodate you.*","eventType":"PHYSICAL","eventUrl":"https://www.meetup.com/greater-toronto-travel-and-social-club/events/316755853/","isSaved":false,"maxTickets":0,"rsvpState":"JOIN_OPEN","featuredEventPhoto":{"__ref":"PhotoInfo:536123166"},"displayPhoto":{"__ref":"PhotoInfo:536123166"},"feeSettings":null,"socialProofInsights":null,"rsvps":{"__typename":"RsvpConnection","totalCount":5,"edges":[{"__typename":"RsvpEdge","node":{"__typename":"Rsvp","isHost":true,"member":{"__ref":"Member:301080506"}}},{"__typename":"RsvpEdge","node":{"__typename":"Rsvp","isHost":true,"member":{"__ref":"Member:234021075"}}},{"__typename":"RsvpEdge","node":{"__typename":"Rsvp","isHost":true,"member":{"__ref":"Member:367966970"}}},{"__typename":"RsvpEdge","node":{"__typename":"Rsvp","isHost":true,"member":{"__ref":"Member:94711032"}}},{"__typename":"RsvpEdge","node":{"